{% slide title="Case 1: The ticket price" align="center" hideNavigation=false %}
{% columns %}
{% column %}
"How much is a bus ticket in Rome?"

Listen carefully to the answer from the assistant.

Do you think this answer is right or wrong?

Now we check the answer in a second place.

Open the website of the Rome buses.

Is the price the same in both places?
{% /column %}
{% column %}
![slide_2_Freeform_8.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_2_Freeform_8.png)

![slide_2_Freeform_9.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_2_Freeform_9.png)
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /slide %}

{% slide title="Case 2: The strike" align="center" hideNavigation=false %}
{% columns %}
{% column %}
"Are the trains to Florence normal tomorrow?"

Listen carefully to the answer from the assistant.

Do you think this answer is right or wrong?

Now we check the answer in a second place.

The trainer opens the train app or website.

Is there a strike tomorrow, yes or no?
{% /column %}
{% column %}
![slide_3_Freeform_7.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_3_Freeform_7.png)
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /slide %}

{% slide title="Ask for changes" align="center" hideNavigation=false %}
{% columns %}
{% column %}
Add one sentence at the end of your question.

"Tell me what can change. Tell me where to check."

The trainer asks the same question again now.

"Are the trains to Florence normal tomorrow?
Tell me what can change. Tell me where to check."

What is different in the new answer now?

Always check important travel information in a second place.
{% /column %}
{% column %}
![slide_4_Freeform_7.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_4_Freeform_7.png)
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /slide %}

{% slide title="Why can the assistant be wrong?" align="center" hideNavigation=false %}
{% columns %}
{% column %}
![slide_5_Freeform_7.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_5_Freeform_7.png)

![slide_5_Freeform_8.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_5_Freeform_8.png)

![slide_5_Freeform_9.png](@admin-assets/images/courses/6-5/slide_5_Freeform_9.png)
{% /column %}
{% column %}
- The AI learned its information some time ago.
- New information is not always inside the assistant. Prices and strikes can change very often during the year.
- The assistant can give you old information about them.
- Some assistants can also search the internet for you. Try to turn the research on.
- Answers from the internet can also be wrong sometimes.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
